            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of phaeohyphomycosis in a three-year-old female child born to consanguineous parents is reported. The causative agent was Exophiala jmmlmei. The lesions were found in skin, subcutaneous tissue, lymph nodes and limb bones, which makes it a rare case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
